    {
      "text": "do not sound a trumpet … as the hypocrites, Matt. 6:2 (3 Ne. 13:2). thou prayest, thou shalt not be as the hypocrites, Matt. 6:5 (3 Ne. 13:5). when ye fast, be not, as the hypocrites, Matt. 6:16. Thou hypocrite, first cast out the beam, Matt. 7:5 (Luke 6:42; 3 Ne. 14:5). come to you in sheep’s clothing, but inwardly they are ravening wolves, Matt. 7:15 (3 Ne. 14:15). Ye hypocrites, well did Esaias prophesy of you, Matt. 15:7 (Mark 7:6). O ye hypocrites, ye can discern the face of the sky, Matt. 16:3 (Luke 12:56). said, I go, sir: and went not, Matt. 21:30. Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites, Matt. 23:23 (Luke 11:44). within ye are full of hypocrisy, Matt. 23:28. appoint him his portion with the hypocrites, Matt. 24:51 (JS—M 1:54). clean the outside … but your inward part is full, Luke 11:39. leaven of the Pharisees, which is hypocrisy, Luke 12:1. hypocrite, doth not each one of you on the sabbath loose, Luke 13:15. teachest another, teachest thou not thyself, Rom. 2:21. shall they call on him in whom they have not believed, Rom. 10:14. Speaking lies in hypocrisy, 1 Tim. 4:2. profess that they know God; but in works they deny him, Titus 1:16. Out of the same mouth proceedeth blessing and cursing, James 3:10. laying aside all … hypocrisies, 1 Pet. 2:1.",
